# Modern Soft Wrapping & Zero Tracking

The refinement of typography surfaces in the subtlest line breaks and letter spacing. Arbitrary manual breaks and loose tracking silently degrade interface quality.

## The Visual Flaw of Typographic Orphans

In descriptive cards or modals, a paragraph frequently concludes with **a single orphan word or lonely punctuation mark trailing on the final line**.
These orphans unbalance the bottom boundary of the paragraph, leaving awkward negative space that reads unpolished.

## Modern CSS Soft Wrapping: pretty and balance

From Chrome 117+ and Safari 17.4+ onward, browser engines feature dynamic programming wrapping algorithms. TuffEx establishes them as system defaults:

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="scss"}
---
code: |
  // 1. Headings and short titles (≤6 lines): Balanced line variance
  .tx-heading,
  .tx-modal__title {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  // 2. Body prose and descriptions: Orphan prevention
  .tx-prose p,
  .tx-description {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
---
:::

- `text-wrap: balance`: The layout engine minimizes character variance across lines, rendering harmonious inverted-pyramid or balanced blocks.
- `text-wrap: pretty`: Targets terminal orphans. When a single trailing word is detected, it pulls the preceding word down to form a balanced couplet.

## Banning Hardcoded Line Breaks

**Injecting artificial `<br>` or `\n` into dynamic copy is strictly prohibited**!
Hard breaks hardcode current viewport assumptions into text models. When users resize windows, hard breaks split sentences prematurely, destroying readability. Wrapping belongs strictly to the engine's soft-breaking algorithms.

## Zero Tracking on Body Copy and Permitted Exceptions

Type foundries spend years tuning kerning pairs (e.g. `AV`, `To`, `We`). Injecting `letter-spacing: 1px` onto body text shatters these optical locks, decreasing reading comprehension velocity by over 20%.

TuffEx mandates: **Zero tracking on body text**. Letter-spacing is permitted strictly across three edge cases:
1. **≤11px Uppercase Micro-labels** (`TxSidebarNav` headers at `0.08em`): Prevents small caps from collapsing together.
2. **≥20px Display Numerals** (`TxInsightMetric` at `-0.01em`): Tightens oversized numerals.
3. **Centered Avatar Initials**: The glyph functions as graphic art rather than prose.
